##Install QIIME2 on your Linux distribution (Ubuntu 24.04)##

Installing miniconda (verify the python version, with --version, and download the correct, i.e. Miniconda3-py312_25.7.0-2-Linux-x86_64.sh)

#Check that all packages are up to date
sudo apt update

#Upgrade Ubuntu
sudo apt upgrade

Copy the .sh file in Ubuntu folder and launch with bash command

After the installation, close and reopen Ubuntu

If all works, you can see <base> before your name

#Check if conda is installed
conda list

#Update the conda environment
conda update conda

#Install wget package
conda install wget

#Install QIIME2 (amplicon distribution)
conda env create -n qiime2-amplicon-2024.10 --file https://data.qiime2.org/distro/amplicon/qiime2-amplicon-2024.10-py310-linux-conda.yml
(There are others qiime2 distribution to do other things like metagenome, pathogenome, tiny distribution)

Now everytime you launch ubuntu you need to activate qiime2 with:
conda activate qiime2-amplicon-2024.10
